WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:03.697
This briefing comes from
Zero Trust and Assessment,

3
00:00:03.697 --> 00:00:06.837
one of the books of the
Federal Modernization Workbook.

4
00:00:06.837 --> 00:00:11.000
It's about how an agency measures
its Zero Trust posture across every

5
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.088
estate it runs, and then turns what
the tools find into a real program.

6
00:00:15.088 --> 00:00:16.463
We'll take four questions.

7
00:00:16.463 --> 00:00:19.262
Why is Zero Trust a whole-agency property?

8
00:00:19.262 --> 00:00:21.775
What do the mandates and
tools actually cover?

9
00:00:21.775 --> 00:00:23.175
Who owns the posture?

10
00:00:23.175 --> 00:00:24.512
And how do you assess it?

11
00:00:24.512 --> 00:00:29.280
If you keep one idea, keep this
one: unify first, assess second,

12
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.562
and treat every tool as
evidence, never as the verdict.

13
00:00:33.562 --> 00:00:38.637
The slides and notes carry every detail
and source; I'll stick to what matters.

14
00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:42.050
Let's start with why one score
has to cover the whole agency.
